</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134636724,imgsize-733079.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Georgia begins 10-year forest restoration at 132-acre Towaliga Preserve with data-centre partnership]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134638691.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Towaliga Preserve is about to launch an ambitious 10-year forest restoration project, backed by QTS Data Centres. This significant initiative aims to revitalize 132 acres, focusing on ecosystem management and biodiversity enhancement. Throughout the decade, contractors will engage in tasks like invasive species control and planting native trees. After the project, the Southern Conservation Trust will ensure the area remains cared for and healthy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/georgia-has-begun-a-10-year-restoration-of-132-acres-at-towaliga-preserve-using-a-data-centre-partnership-to-rebuild-forest-habitat-on-one-of-henry-countys-largest-undeveloped-properties/articleshow/134638691.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/georgia-has-begun-a-10-year-restoration-of-132-acres-at-towaliga-preserve-using-a-data-centre-partnership-to-rebuild-forest-habitat-on-one-of-henry-countys-largest-undeveloped-properties/articleshow/134638691.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T21:07:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134638770,imgsize-1482218.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['No deadline for Sheikh Hasina's return', says Indian high commissioner in Bangladesh]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134661882.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[High Commissioner Dinesh Trivedi addressed the extradition request for Sheikh Hasina from Bangladesh, stating that the matter is under legal review, preventing a set timeline for her repatriation. He clarified that India had no involvement in her arrival, citing the dire circumstances in Bangladesh. As relations between India and Bangladesh grow increasingly strained, the new Bangladeshi government remains resolute in pursuing Hasina's extradition.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-deadline-for-sheikh-hasinas-return-says-indian-high-commissioner-in-bangladesh/articleshow/134661882.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-deadline-for-sheikh-hasinas-return-says-indian-high-commissioner-in-bangladesh/articleshow/134661882.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T20:36:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134662005,imgsize-135808.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian man with US Green Card challenges his immigration detention; DHS reveals his criminal record in court]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134661969.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-man-with-us-green-card-challenges-his-immigration-detention-dhs-reveals-his-criminal-record-in-court/articleshow/134661969.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-man-with-us-green-card-challenges-his-immigration-detention-dhs-reveals-his-criminal-record-in-court/articleshow/134661969.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T20:41:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134661983,imgsize-57126.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Wisconsin diver finds 17-foot canoe underwater, radiocarbon dating puts it at 1,000 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134634887.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A fascinating discovery was made by diver Mark Schachtner: an ancient dugout canoe dating back about 1,000 years in Pewaukee Lake. In partnership with Native Nations, the Wisconsin Historical Society is carefully documenting this important archaeological treasure. Researchers have assessed its condition and theorized its submersion history. This find not only contributes to Wisconsin's storied history of ancient canoes but also sheds light on Indigenous practices.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/wisconsin-diver-mark-schachtner-was-searching-pewaukee-lake-for-old-bottles-when-he-spotted-a-17-foot-canoe-15-feet-underwater-radiocarbon-dating-has-now-confirmed-it-is-about-1000-years-old/articleshow/134634887.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/wisconsin-diver-mark-schachtner-was-searching-pewaukee-lake-for-old-bottles-when-he-spotted-a-17-foot-canoe-15-feet-underwater-radiocarbon-dating-has-now-confirmed-it-is-about-1000-years-old/articleshow/134634887.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T19:47:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134635073,imgsize-122983.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michigan commits $89 million to restore polluted Detroit and Kalamazoo rivers by 2040]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134637191.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Michigan's Reclaim the Rivers initiative is set to invest $89 million to tackle pollution in the Detroit and Kalamazoo rivers. This funding is dedicated to sediment removal, restoring habitats, and increasing public access for recreation. State officials envision a significant transformation by 2040, working to reverse years of industrial damage and improve water quality and ecological health across communities and the Great Lakes.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/decades-of-industrial-pollution-left-michigans-detroit-and-kalamazoo-rivers-contaminated-with-pcbs-mercury-and-other-chemicals-the-state-is-now-committing-89-million-to-clean-and-restore-the-waterways-by-2040/articleshow/134637191.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/decades-of-industrial-pollution-left-michigans-detroit-and-kalamazoo-rivers-contaminated-with-pcbs-mercury-and-other-chemicals-the-state-is-now-committing-89-million-to-clean-and-restore-the-waterways-by-2040/articleshow/134637191.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T19:46:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134637388,imgsize-292550.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Adopted man discovers Grammy winner Michael McDonald is his biological father]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134635421.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A St. Louis man adopted as a baby nearly 60 years ago discovered that Grammy-winning musician Michael McDonald was his biological father after a previously unknown half-brother took a 23andMe DNA test. The discovery led to meetings with both his birth mother and McDonald, followed by a family reunion that also introduced McDonald to his grandchildren.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/st-louis-man-michael-goessling-was-adopted-nearly-60-years-ago-after-an-unknown-half-brother-took-a-23andme-test-he-learned-five-time-grammy-winner-michael-mcdonald-was-his-biological-father/articleshow/134635421.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/st-louis-man-michael-goessling-was-adopted-nearly-60-years-ago-after-an-unknown-half-brother-took-a-23andme-test-he-learned-five-time-grammy-winner-michael-mcdonald-was-his-biological-father/articleshow/134635421.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T19:45:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134635725,imgsize-55852.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Canada's largest gold heist of 2023: 'Fugitive' Simran Preet Panesar can't leave India; 'If he's hiding, he's hiding in plain daylight']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134661045.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/canadas-largest-gold-heist-of-2023-fugitive-simran-preet-panesar-cant-leave-india-if-hes-hiding-hes-hiding-in-plain-daylight/articleshow/134661045.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/canadas-largest-gold-heist-of-2023-fugitive-simran-preet-panesar-cant-leave-india-if-hes-hiding-hes-hiding-in-plain-daylight/articleshow/134661045.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T19:25:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134661088,imgsize-19148.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[57 new deep-sea species discovered in Argentina’s Mar del Plata Canyon, including ‘Loki’ sea cucumber]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134635884.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a groundbreaking deep-sea voyage off Argentina, scientists uncovered 57 brand new marine species alongside five previously unclassified genera. Using a remotely operated vehicle, they pulled samples from the Mar del Plata Submarine Canyon. Among these marine marvels was a unique and translucent sea cucumber whimsically dubbed Loki. A subsequent collaborative workshop was instrumental in accelerating the species identification process, highlighting the astonishing biodiversity of the South Atlantic's deep ecosystems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/scientists-identified-57-new-deep-sea-species-from-argentinas-mar-del-plata-canyon-including-a-translucent-sea-cucumber-nicknamed-loki-after-remotely-operated-vehicles-explored-the-depths/articleshow/134635884.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/scientists-identified-57-new-deep-sea-species-from-argentinas-mar-del-plata-canyon-including-a-translucent-sea-cucumber-nicknamed-loki-after-remotely-operated-vehicles-explored-the-depths/articleshow/134635884.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T19:12:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134636111,imgsize-135707.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Cleveland factory once tied to auto history sells for $300,000, avoiding demolition]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134634830.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-cleveland-factory-once-belonged-to-americas-largest-gasoline-car-maker-and-faced-demolition-this-year-a-developer-has-now-bought-the-7-3-acre-260000-sq-ft-complex-for-300000-and-plans-to-reuse-it/articleshow/134634830.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-cleveland-factory-once-belonged-to-americas-largest-gasoline-car-maker-and-faced-demolition-this-year-a-developer-has-now-bought-the-7-3-acre-260000-sq-ft-complex-for-300000-and-plans-to-reuse-it/articleshow/134634830.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T19:12:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134634880,imgsize-419322.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[6 missing after Gulfstream jet disappears near Nantucket after takeoff from Bermuda]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134660618.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/6-missing-after-gulfstream-jet-disappears-near-nantucket-after-takeoff-from-bermuda/articleshow/134660618.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/6-missing-after-gulfstream-jet-disappears-near-nantucket-after-takeoff-from-bermuda/articleshow/134660618.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T18:55:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134660692,imgsize-137654.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[DJ Alok has helped restore 3 million sq m of native forest in Brazil]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134658369.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/brazilian-dj-alok-has-helped-restore-3-million-sq-m-of-native-forest-across-brazil-400000-seedlings-have-been-planted/articleshow/134658369.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/brazilian-dj-alok-has-helped-restore-3-million-sq-m-of-native-forest-across-brazil-400000-seedlings-have-been-planted/articleshow/134658369.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T17:03:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134658415,imgsize-109750.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A Moroccan mine built a road from phosphate waste rock; field tests cut dust emissions by 91%]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134658013.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Morocco, a phosphate mine has implemented an innovative road surface made from waste rock generated during phosphate extraction. This robust, three-layered pavement design not only successfully supports heavy mining vehicles but also helps manage dust emissions effectively. Testing resulted in a notable decrease in airborne dust and enhanced road quality, with an anticipated 15 percent boost in productivity for mining operations, while also cutting down maintenance expenses.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-moroccan-mine-built-a-heavy-truck-road-from-phosphate-waste-rock-field-tests-cut-dust-emissions-by-91/articleshow/134658013.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-moroccan-mine-built-a-heavy-truck-road-from-phosphate-waste-rock-field-tests-cut-dust-emissions-by-91/articleshow/134658013.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T17:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134658396,imgsize-99780.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida sea captain spent years searching before buying a Scottish castle]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134658365.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-florida-sea-captain-spent-3-years-searching-for-a-scottish-castle-he-bought-one-built-after-a-family-feud-and-said-to-be-haunted/articleshow/134658365.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-florida-sea-captain-spent-3-years-searching-for-a-scottish-castle-he-bought-one-built-after-a-family-feud-and-said-to-be-haunted/articleshow/134658365.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T17:43:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134659454,imgsize-237332.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How a US pest-control effort turned Asian lady beetles into an invasive species]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134659624.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Originally imported to the United States for biological pest control, the multicoloured Asian lady beetle, or Harmonia axyridis, has turned invasive. Competing with native ladybugs, this species disrupts ecosystems. While it helps manage aphid populations, its autumn behavior drives adult beetles to invade homes, creating an unwanted nuisance. This case serves as a cautionary tale about the unintended effects of introducing nonnative species into local environments.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1916-the-us-began-releasing-asian-lady-beetles-to-control-aphids-and-scale-insects-decades-later-harmonia-axyridis-became-invasive-and-was-linked-to-declines-of-native-ladybirds/articleshow/134659624.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1916-the-us-began-releasing-asian-lady-beetles-to-control-aphids-and-scale-insects-decades-later-harmonia-axyridis-became-invasive-and-was-linked-to-declines-of-native-ladybirds/articleshow/134659624.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T17:58:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134659673,imgsize-101778.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Adult Homo erectus fossil confirms species appeared in Africa 2 million years ago]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134633416.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Researchers have described 18 previously unpublished hominin fossils from South Africa, including an adultHomo erectusfossil dated to 2 million years ago. The findings support the species’ first appearance in southern Africa at that time and provide evidence of microevolution inP. robustus.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/researchers-described-18-previously-unpublished-hominin-fossils-from-south-africa-including-an-adult-homo-erectus-dated-to-2-million-years-ago-200000-years-older-than-other-known-adult-fossils/articleshow/134633416.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/researchers-described-18-previously-unpublished-hominin-fossils-from-south-africa-including-an-adult-homo-erectus-dated-to-2-million-years-ago-200000-years-older-than-other-known-adult-fossils/articleshow/134633416.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T18:09:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134633695,imgsize-105024.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California tech company owner arrested over alleg